{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"generated":true,"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"}],"metadata":{"title":"Choosing a storage","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage"]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus"},{"text":", and know what changes.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in one of two storages, chosen when it is created:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let nexus = Nexus()                       \/\/ the default, same as Nexus(storage: .archetype)","let churning = Nexus(storage: .sparseSet) \/\/ for heavy add\/remove churn"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both storages offer the same API with the same observable behavior: generational entity identifiers, events, the structural lock and its traps, families, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"type":"text","text":", spans, snapshots, cloning and the entity state machine. Every test of the package runs against both. What differs is where the components live in memory, and with it what is cheap."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Nexus()"},{"type":"text","text":" uses it. Choose "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" explicitly for workloads dominated by heavy component add and remove churn (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). There is no storage protocol: the set of storages is closed, and a nexus switches on its storage once per call, so each storage compiles to concrete code."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The sparse-set storage","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-sparse-set-storage"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps one dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type that maps an entity to its slot in that array, and a bitset of component types per entity. Adding or removing a component touches the data of that one type only, and no other component moves. Looking up one component is a sparse index read plus an array read."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family is the weak spot: the members of a family are stored in each component array in the order the components were added, so every extra component type costs a lookup per member, and the reads are scattered once the arrays were shuffled by churn."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-archetype-storage","level":3,"text":"The archetype storage"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" follows the design of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","isActive":true},{"text":": entities with exactly the same component types live in one table, with a column (an array) per component type. An index maps every entity to its table and row. Tables are created when a component set appears first, and adding or removing one component type moves the entity’s row to another table along a cached edge of the table graph.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterating a family visits the tables that match it, and walks their columns linearly: no lookup per member and a sequential read per component. The list of matching tables is cached per family, which the nexus lists when the family is created and extends when a new table appears. A table that became empty stays alive, along with its columns and its entry in the cached lists, where an iteration skips it. Cleaning the nexus with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()"},{"text":" drops all tables.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In flecs this is the default, and sparse components are the opt-in trait (","type":"text"},{"code":"Sparse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"): “Sparse components are stored outside of tables, which means they do not have to be moved”, trading query speed for component add and remove speed (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md"},{"text":"). Fireblade 1.x was the reverse, a sparse set per component type; the two storages make that a choice per nexus instead of per component.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"What-the-numbers-say","level":3,"text":"What the numbers say"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Measured with 10 000 entities, release build, Apple silicon, wall clock p50 per pass (","type":"text"},{"code":"make benchmark","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", see ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Benchmarks\/"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}]},{"header":"row","alignments":["left","right","right"],"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Case"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sparse set","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Archetype"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2.5 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"18 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"4.3 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B, C, D)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"31 μs"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"7.7 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, writing: B)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"17 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"4.4 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, writing: C)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"23 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"6.1 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 10% of the entities match","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"3.6 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"1.3 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 100 000 entities with shuffled storage order","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"227 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"27 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 1 024 different component sets"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"18 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter pack, 5 reads and 2 writes"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2 200 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1 800 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":" over a family, 2 components"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Random ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entity.get"},{"type":"text","text":" of one component, 10 000 lookups"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"334 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"345 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a component to each entity and remove it again, 10 000 entities","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2 180 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"4 900 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create and destroy 1 000 entities with 7 components"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 730 μs"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 510 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fireblade 1.x needed 480 μs for the plain iteration of one component and 1 220 μs for two ("},{"code":"IterOnlyOneComponent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"IterOnlyTwoComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). Both storages iterate without any allocation."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterating with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"text":" is 1.6 to 8 times faster on the archetype storage: about 4 times in the plain case, 8 times when the sparse-set arrays are shuffled against each other, and least when the entities are spread over many small tables.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Changing the component set of an entity costs about twice as much on the archetype storage: the whole row moves. An entity that changes its component set less than once in a few frames is far ahead on iteration; a world that toggles a component on most entities every frame is better off with the sparse set.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Plain ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"text":" iteration and random access cost the same on both: they look every component up per entity.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Entity creation and destruction are a bit slower on the archetype storage, because the row of every component moves with the entity.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"text":"Which storage to pick","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Which-storage-to-pick"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default is the archetype storage: it iterates faster (see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say"},{"type":"text","text":"), and iteration is what most worlds spend their time on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off: the archetype storage buys iteration speed with the cost of moving a row whenever the component set of an entity changes. Prefer "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet"},{"type":"text","text":" when the workload is dominated by heavy add and remove churn, for example toggling a component on most entities every frame. This matches flecs, where sparse components are the opt-in trait for components that are added and removed often."}]},{"text":"Differences you can observe","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Differences-you-can-observe"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration order."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The sparse-set storage visits the members of a family in the order of the family’s member list, the archetype storage table by table and row by row, and rows move when entities change tables. Neither order is a contract; use "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" or your own key if you need one."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Single-type spans."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" view one contiguous array. On the archetype storage a type is stored in one column per table, so if entities with different component sets have the type, the span views a temporary copy made table by table (and the writing variant stores it back when the closure returns, also when it throws). That costs one allocation and a copy per call, and nothing can observe the difference while the closure runs, because the type is locked."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Family spans."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" passes one batch per matching table on the archetype storage, however the nexus was used before; the sparse-set storage passes shorter batches after churn. Both visit every member exactly once, and the closure must be correct for any batch size."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the spans."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(reading:_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(reading:_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Gives ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":" read access to all components of a type as one contiguous ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Span"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"componentSpan"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"reading","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type, (","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV","text":"Span"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rethrows","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"componentSpan(reading:_:)"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/clear()":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/clear()","abstract":[{"text":"Clears all data from the Nexus.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clear","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","kind":"symbol","title":"clear()"},"https://www.flecs.dev/flecs/md_docs_2Queries.html":{"type":"link","url":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","title":"flecs","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"flecs","type":"text"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A lightweight, fast and easy to use Entity-Component System in Swift."}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS","title":"FirebladeECS","kind":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventDelegate":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventdelegate","abstract":[{"text":"A delegate for receiving Nexus events and errors.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NexusEventDelegate","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NexusEventDelegate","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"NexusEventDelegate"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/archetype":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/archetype","abstract":[{"text":"One table per component set, a column per component type in every table, an index from entity to table and row.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"archetype"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Nexus.StorageKind.archetype"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/sparseSet":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/sparseset","abstract":[{"text":"One dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type, a bitset per entity.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"sparseSet"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","kind":"symbol","title":"Nexus.StorageKind.sparseSet"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Nexus"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Nexus"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Nexus"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/init(storage:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/init(storage:)","abstract":[{"text":"Initializes a new Nexus.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"storage"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC","text":"Nexus"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC11StorageKindO","text":"StorageKind"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/init(storage:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"init(storage:)"},"https://github.com/SanderMertens/flecs/blob/master/docs/ComponentTraits.md":{"type":"link","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","title":"component traits","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"component traits","type":"text"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Family/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"forEachComponentSpan","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"R1","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W1","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"reading","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"R1","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"writing","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W1","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type, (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Span","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"R1","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableSpan","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s11MutableSpanV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W1","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Void","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rethrows","kind":"keyword"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/family\/foreachcomponentspan(reading:writing:_:)","conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"each C"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Component"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"title":"forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Iterates the members of this family in batches, giving ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":" the components of a batch as contiguous spans.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReadingAndWritingComp